:0.06239572050298895,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":54.1,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.010223046921382237,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.68174005,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"PACS Group, Inc., through its subsidiaries, operates skilled nursing facilities and assisted living facilities in the United States. It also provides senior care and independent living facilities. The company engages in the acquisition, ownership, and leasing of health care-related properties. PACS Group, Inc. was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason  Murray | Co-Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 45 | Compensation: $8.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 47K people. Revenue per employee of $111K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $6K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 78\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["PACS Group, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $7.7B market cap on $5.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +29% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $299M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 10.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 68% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.45854483925549894},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $45.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Financial quality scores above most Healthcare peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Did PACS Group, Inc. Insiders Breach their Fiduciary Duties to Shareholders?","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/did-pacs-group-inc-insiders-breach-their-fiduciary-duties-to-shareholders-302938100.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794503940.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Fifty-Eight PACS Post-Acute Locations Named Top Nursing Homes for 2027 by U.S. News & World Report","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/fifty-eight-pacs-post-acute-194500468.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794339900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"We Think PACS Group's (NYSE:PACS) Robust Earnings Are Conservative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-pacs/pacs-group/news/we-think-pacs-groups-nysepacs-robust-earnings-are-conservati","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794309464.483,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.852,"tier":0,"scope":"company","t